    "long_instructions": "## Explore Line and Bar Charts\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program. Observe the two charts it creates.\r\n\r\n2. Highlight the first chart’s code, from `plt.figure()` through `plt.show()`, and ask AI:\r\n\r\n   > How does this code create, label, and display a line chart? Which data appears on each axis?\r\n\r\n3. Check the AI’s response:\r\n\r\n   - Does the explanation match the chart you observed?\r\n   - Which columns provide the x- and y-axis data?\r\n   - Which lines add the title and axis labels?\r\n\r\n4. Add a `#` comment above `plt.plot()` explaining what the line does.\r\n\r\n5. Repeat these steps with the second chart. Ask AI:\r\n\r\n   > How does this code create, label, and display a bar chart? How is it different from the line-chart code?\r\n\r\n6. Add a `#` comment above `plt.bar()` explaining what the line does.",
